Detailed Task Implementations
Task 1: Refactoring Legacy Code (Smell Removal)
Objective: Identify and eliminate maintainability anti-patterns in a legacy ReportManager class.

Implementation Details:

Replaced inefficient string concatenation loops with streamlined String.join methods.

Eliminated null-unsafe type.equals() conditional branching by introducing polymorphism via the ReportFormatter interface (PdfReportFormatter and CsvReportFormatter).

Decoupled hardcoded static dependencies by injecting the Notifier interface (EmailNotifier) via constructor injection.

Task 2: Fail-Fast and Immutable Boundaries
Objective: Design a defensive, immutable domain model that prevents invalid object states.

Implementation Details:

Created an immutable final domain class BankTransfer encapsulating fromAccount, toAccount, and amount (BigDecimal).

Enforced strict constructor guard clauses using Objects.requireNonNull and positive-value validation (amount > 0), throwing an immediate IllegalArgumentException upon invalid data to stop corruption propagation.

Task 3: Structured Tracing (SLF4J MDC Simulation)
Objective: Implement operational diagnosability in production logs using transaction trace tracking.

Implementation Details:

Implemented PaymentProcessor featuring a charge(String txId, double amount) method that simulates Mapped Diagnostic Context ([TraceID: ...]) log injection.

Employed a try-finally block structure to guarantee context cleanup (Context Cleared), preventing thread pollution and memory leaks in concurrent execution flows.

Task 4: The Automated Quality Gate (JUnit 5)
Objective: Master the Arrange-Act-Assert (AAA) unit testing pattern for isolated, fast feedback loops.

Implementation Details:

Developed OrderService and VipDiscount to process order totals without external database dependencies.

Configured Maven dependencies for JUnit 5 and built an isolated test class (OrderServiceTest) verifying calculateTotal_appliesVipDiscount_withoutTouchingDatabase().

How to Build and Run
Prerequisites
Java Development Kit (JDK): JDK 17 or higher

Build Tool: Apache Maven

IDE: Apache NetBeans (or any Maven-compatible IDE)

Running Tasks 1 – 3 (Console Applications)
Clone the repository:

Bash
git clone <your-repository-url>
Open the Lab9 project in NetBeans.

Expand Source Packages and locate Task1, Task2, or Task3.

Right-click Main.java inside the target task package and select Run File (Shift + F6).

Note: Running Task2.Main intentionally triggers an IllegalArgumentException stack trace as part of the fail-fast demonstration.

Running Task 4 (JUnit 5 Tests)
Navigate to Test Packages -> Task4 -> OrderServiceTest.java in NetBeans.

Right-click OrderServiceTest.java and select Test File (Ctrl + F6), or execute the Maven command line:

Bash
mvn test
